g a defect, clear caches, install software, stage, commit, publish or pin.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-84f437, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-84f437)\nTESTER COMPLETION DIRECTIVE after cancelled RUN-260729-84f437: preserve the current four-file test-only candidate. The successor began the requested rc.5 work but then launched a broad lifecycle gate across install/scopes/globalbins/adapters/managerlock/staging/transaction/protocoljson/cmd with -timeout 1800s while docs PID 13051 was already running cmd/curator, violating the no-overlap and no-timeout-change directives. Orchestrator cancelled the conformance process group; its task-owned gotmp is only 27 MiB and retained as evidence. Spawn an independent Codex tester to audit the exact four-file delta and rc.5 vector mapping immediately, but run no Go command until PID 13051 is terminal. Then use CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260729-3nx97g/worktree/conformance/v1 and only narrow -count=1 godriver/skillspec/interop tests, followed by build/vet/gofmt/diff as disk permits. Do not run cmd/curator package, install/lifecycle aggregates, a full suite, race aggregate or altered timeout in this pass. Attach exact coverage/gap evidence and route to review if the candidate satisfies AC; route to development with concrete missing vectors otherwise. No product edits, cache clearing, host install, stage, commit, publish or pin.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; d